Smart Mobility
Traffic System Analysis and Action Plan Proposal in the City of Gradiška

Through the SMILE project, the City of Gradiška has become one of the first cities in Bosnia and Herzegovina to align its vision for the development of the urban transport system with the principles of sustainable mobility.

The general objectives of the SMILE project, which can be effectively applied in Gradiška, include:

Supporting transport policies aimed at reducing greenhouse gas emissions from the transportation sector;

Improving environmental conditions in high-traffic urban areas;

Optimizing the impact of human activities on land, air, and public health.

As part of the activity plan, a summary of proposed actions has been developed to support the implementation of sustainable mobility measures in the City of Gradiška, specifically in the following areas:

Development of the street network and improvement of traffic flow conditions;

Parking policy and system enhancements;

Development and promotion of pedestrian and bicycle transport infrastructure;

Improvement of public transportation services across the city.
